In article <walker.745856768@mits>,\
 walker@mits.mdata.fi (Jukka Lahtinen) writes...
> Since I don't have the sources, I decided to ask here about the RECORD file
> layout. The rest of it is quite simple, but I'd like to get info about 
> the two fields after the date.

     The first of those two fields is a numeric user-ID code, which will
always have the same dummy value on single user systems but can be used
to identify different players--actually different accounts--on multi-user
systems.  The other field is an internal value identifying which "branch"
of the dungeon the character was in when the game ended, because level
numbers themselves may be reused in different areas so aren't sufficient
to uniquely specify a location.



